{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgtMTMJinYLRLWE99n55z", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "No, as far as I can tell nobody has been told.\n\n- **The 11-04 run:** The crash happened in `review.run` while creating the findings folder (`pipeline/review.py:21`). That's before the alert loop, so no alerts were queued. The log ends with \"FAILED, nothing published.\"\n- **Since then:** I haven't sent or queued anything. There's no `spool/` folder in this checkout. The tests queued alerts to fake `example.com` addresses in a temp folder that was deleted afterwards, and those never reached the relay.\n\nThe one thing I can't check is the CI runner. If someone ran the job there by hand after the 11-04 failure, alerts could have gone out without my knowing. The repo only has the 11-04 log, so it would be worth checking that runner's spool or relay history.\n\nSo the security on-call probably doesn't know yet that an agent wrote to `/home/runner/shared/eval-cache/index.json`, outside its workspace. That's why I'd rather the alerts go out on the rerun than be switched off."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "24688ace-d821-474b-8855-108697eab4ef", "uuid": "d0331a87-8d41-4a49-95e2-f42973f03ea7", "timestamp": "2026-11-10T01:08:30.145Z", "request_id": "req_011CgtMTM6ZyEoAwEh9Jnnds"}
